---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Contact"
  description="How to contact China AI Hub: email, WhatsApp, and the public issue tracker for corrections."
  type="article"
>
  <article class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h1>Contact</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">Last updated: 2026-10-23</p>

    <h2>Contact point</h2>
    <p>
      China AI Hub is operated by the China AI Hub project, researched and written by the
      <a href="/authors/">SinoAI Hub Research Team</a>. The primary contact point is:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Email</strong> — <a href="mailto:admin@sinoaihub.com">admin@sinoaihub.com</a></li>
      <li><strong>WhatsApp</strong> — <a href="https://wa.me/8613323237275" rel="noopener" target="_blank">wa.me/8613323237275</a></li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The site has <strong>no contact form</strong> and no live chat; please use the channels above.
      The WhatsApp button opens WhatsApp's platform, and any conversation there is governed by
      WhatsApp's own terms and privacy policy.
    </p>

    <h2>What to contact us about</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Corrections and data errors</strong> — the fastest route is the
        <a href="/corrections/">corrections policy</a>, which explains exactly what to include (page
        URL, the wrong value, and the correct value with an official source link).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Content or research questions</strong> — questions about how a fact was sourced or
        verified, or about the site's analysis.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Data reuse and licensing</strong> — requests to reuse or republish content beyond
        short attributed quotation; see the <a href="/data-policy/">Data Policy</a> and the
        <a href="/terms/">Terms of Use</a> first.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Privacy matters</strong> — questions or requests about your information; see the
        <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Public issue tracker</h2>
    <p>
      For corrections you may also open an issue on the public project repository:
      <a href="https://github.com/martinxionbiotech-max/china-ai-hub/issues" rel="noopener" target="_blank">github.com/martinxionbiotech-max/china-ai-hub/issues</a>.
      This is the same channel referenced in the <a href="/corrections/">corrections policy</a>, and
      it reaches the same team as the email above. It is the preferred channel for corrections
      because it keeps the record public.
    </p>

    <h2>Response expectations</h2>
    <p>
      We aim to acknowledge correspondence within a few working days, and to act on verified
      corrections within a few working days as well. The site is maintained alongside other research
      work, so response times can vary. Data on Chinese AI pricing and releases changes quickly;
      periodic re-verification cycles run in addition to ad-hoc corrections, as described in the
      <a href="/data-policy/">Data Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Before you write</h2>
    <p>
      Please note that China AI Hub does not provide professional, investment, procurement, legal or
      security advice, and cannot advise on which model or API to buy — see the
      <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a>. For vendor-specific questions (pricing, licensing,
      availability, data residency), the authoritative source is the vendor itself; the site links
      to each vendor's official documentation on the relevant entity pages.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
